Subject: [PATCH 6/6] panfrost: kbase backend stays selectable via
 PAN_KMOD_RESTRICT_TO_BACKENDS

No code change: documents and locks the backend-selection contract
the kbase backend (0001) already implements, which the v5.2 compat
work (0005) must not break.

- Backend table order in pan_kmod.c is panfrost, panthor, kbase
  (kbase LAST): a DRM render node is adopted by panfrost_kmod first;
  kbase only sees fds the DRM backends refuse (its dev_create
  rejects any fd answering drmGetVersion, unless the H2-shim adapt
  patch from code/userspace/gpu/mesa-render applies, which probes
  the UK handshake on a dup first).
- PAN_KMOD_RESTRICT_TO_BACKENDS (pan_kmod.c, DEBUG_GET_ONCE_OPTION,
  default "all") selects backends: "panfrost" forces the DRM path
  (H1/stock panfrost_dri.so, no Mesa patches needed beyond 0005),
  "kbase" forces the kbase UK path (/dev/mali0, needs 0001+0004),
  "all" tries each backend in table order until one adopts the fd.
- 0005 routes get_param/submit through the v52 shim INSIDE
  panfrost_kmod.c (call-site swaps, no hook-table change), so the
  selection logic in pan_kmod.c is untouched: forcing either backend
  still works, and the H2 render-node adapt patch (dev_create fd
  adoption hunk) composes without conflict (different function).

Provenance: 0001 added the kbase table entry + optional
submit_job/jm_ctx_create/jm_ctx_destroy hooks; 0002 made the Gallium
submit/context paths hook-neutral.  This patch adds no hunks so
there is nothing to rebase when those evolve.
